+## 2026-11-06: 0212 installed/tested then original bundle restored; combined YUV blocker confirmed
+- Native Metal CI 42205828792 SUCCESS; source 89b4f2126e983d95b56f0f6b46600ff76d126a3a. All 6 legacy artifact file hashes and ARM64 Mach-O headers verified. Update tar SHA256 c161c79a4b048112b9d9e692cb381924257dce6ae1ee312d5a0494ba87426c77. Staging hashes passed on phone; prior installed bundle matched host backup before activation.
+- Activated staged bundle with original preserved, restarted compositor; normal UI rendering/async completion observed, no graphics crash. Media/audio/Wi-Fi daemons left running. However USER video still dark with Bluetooth audio; reported blurred app-switcher previews.
+- Restored original graphics bundle, retained failed build at .SweetMetal2-0212-failed, restarted graphics. Verified all 6 restored file hashes match pre-update backup. USER then clarified blur was already present on the previous bundle and persists. Do not attribute the blur's origin to 0212. Kernel remains 0211; Bluetooth audio remains the known working output.
+- New 0212 log evidence: separate R8/RG8 plane imports now possible, but CoreAnimation asks Metal format 500 for both NV12 420v video (640x360) and 420f preview-sized surfaces (787x1705). Requests refused by existing format table. Format 500 is combined YCBCR8_420_2P per primary WebKit MetalSPI.h. Supporting independent plane views is insufficient; combined YUV resource/sampler support is required. Common cause of video/preview symptoms is supported by these refusals, not established for every preview.
+- Research must use pinned Mesa25.0.7, not the local mesa-gles-reference (27.0.0-devel) or sweet-metal2-verify (26.2.0-devel); latter versions have multi-plane support that cannot be assumed present in the pinned build. No RGB reinterpretation or unverified color conversion installed.
+- Primary source: https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/main/Source/WebGPU/WebGPU/MetalSPI.h . Speaker path still unfinished, not changed during this trial.
+
 ## 2026-11-06: 0212 native Metal build running; original bundle backed up
 - Reviewed userspace fix/checker/workflow committed 89b4f2126e983d95b56f0f6b46600ff76d126a3a on codex/media-0212, pushed to DC28088/ios-sweet. Native Metal CI run 42205828792 in progress; its new portable planar-layout check passed and full AIR/freedreno bundle build started. Kernel build not required for this userspace change.
 - Existing phone selects /System/Library/Extensions/SweetMetal2.bundle (legacy alias), about 8.5 MiB. Saved a readable 6-file host backup tar with per-file SHA256 inventory under private work/audio-runtime/SweetMetal2-before-0212-private.*. No installed bundle replaced yet; root free about 88 MiB, enough for a similarly sized staged bundle but recheck before install.
